 - **Limitations:** Requires pre-computation of valid cases and does not directly generate geometry; it validates or guides the generation process [S1].
 
 ## Background
-The method was introduced in [S1] to model the geometric behavior of isosurfaces generated by the Marching Cubes algorithm. It builds on the concept of contour spectra [CS07] and was used to prove the completeness of Nielson's cases and model watertight Marching Cubes cases [MSS94]. It addresses the ambiguity of the trilinear interpolant by constraining the possible paths through the case space [S1].
